{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Format & lint on save",
  "description": "When an app source file is saved, format it and check it against the design-system and kid-safety steering rules.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.html",
      "*.css",
      "*.js"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A source file was just saved. 1) Format it consistently: 2-space indentation, double quotes in JS and HTML attributes, semicolons in JS, no trailing whitespace, final newline. If Prettier is available (npx prettier), run `npx prettier --write <file>`; otherwise apply the same rules by hand. 2) Lint: report undeclared variables, unused functions, and console.log left behind. 3) Kid-safety lint per .kiro/steering/kid-safety.md: flag any fetch/XMLHttpRequest/WebSocket/sendBeacon, external URLs in script/link/img src, input fields that ask for personal information, and shame copy (e.g. 'failed', 'lost your streak', 'missed!'). 4) Design lint per .kiro/steering/design-system.md: flag hard-coded hex colours outside the :root palette and interactive elements smaller than 56x56px. Fix formatting directly; list lint findings briefly and do not change behaviour without asking."
  }
}
